{
  "$comment": [
    "Voice corpus definition. Plan: docs/VOICE_STT_TTS_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md §24 (R3, R9).",
    "",
    "TWO KINDS OF ENTRY, and conflating them would invalidate the Phase 0 decision:",
    "",
    "  source: 'synthetic' — generated by scripts/voice-fixtures.mjs from Piper.",
    "    SMOKE ONLY. TTS output is unrealistically clean: no room tone, no",
    "    breath, no clipping, no accent, and a phoneme distribution that came",
    "    from the same espeak rules a recogniser finds easy. It proves the",
    "    pipeline moves bytes. It CANNOT decide the backend bake-off (§6.1),",
    "    cannot set the R2 accuracy thresholds, and cannot clear the R3",
    "    zero-false-authorization gate.",
    "",
    "  source: 'recorded' — a human speaking into a real microphone. These are",
    "    the only entries that count for Phase 0. Record them with",
    "    `node scripts/voice-fixtures.mjs --list` as the script.",
    "",
    "`expect` carries the R9 semantic assertions, so a backend swap is compared",
    "deterministically instead of by ear."
  ],
  "entries": [
    {
      "id": "en-cmd-approve",
      "language": "en",
      "text": "approve",
      "source": "synthetic",
      "voice": "en_US-amy-medium",
      "expect": { "grammar": "approve", "critical": ["approve"] }
    },
    {
      "id": "en-cmd-approve-negated",
      "language": "en",
      "text": "do not approve that",
      "source": "synthetic",
      "voice": "en_US-amy-medium",
      "expect": { "grammar": null, "critical": ["not", "approve"], "negation": true }
    },
    {
      "id": "en-cmd-deny",
      "language": "en",
      "text": "deny",
      "source": "synthetic",
      "voice": "en_US-amy-medium",
      "expect": { "grammar": "deny", "critical": ["deny"] }
    },
    {
      "id": "en-cmd-cancel-negated",
      "language": "en",
      "text": "do not cancel",
      "source": "synthetic",
      "voice": "en_US-amy-medium",
      "expect": { "grammar": null, "critical": ["not", "cancel"], "negation": true }
    },
    {
      "id": "en-cmd-stop-qualified",
      "language": "en",
      "text": "stop after this finishes",
      "source": "synthetic",
      "voice": "en_US-amy-medium",
      "expect": { "grammar": null, "critical": ["stop", "after"], "negation": true }
    },
    {
      "id": "en-cmd-yes-negated",
      "language": "en",
      "text": "I said no, not yes",
      "source": "synthetic",
      "voice": "en_US-amy-medium",
      "expect": { "grammar": null, "critical": ["no", "not", "yes"], "negation": true }
    },
    {
      "id": "en-verb-keep",
      "language": "en",
      "text": "keep the changes",
      "source": "synthetic",
      "voice": "en_US-amy-medium",
      "expect": { "grammar": null, "critical": ["keep"], "mustNotContain": ["undo"] }
    },
    {
      "id": "en-verb-read",
      "language": "en",
      "text": "read the config file",
      "source": "synthetic",
      "voice": "en_US-amy-medium",
      "expect": { "grammar": null, "critical": ["read"], "mustNotContain": ["write"] }
    },
    {
      "id": "en-prompt-identifiers",
      "language": "en",
      "text": "open src slash voice slash VoiceIngress dot ts and check the admission rule",
      "source": "synthetic",
      "voice": "en_US-amy-medium",
      "expect": { "grammar": null, "critical": ["voice", "admission"] }
    },
    {
      "id": "en-prompt-technical",
      "language": "en",
      "text": "restart the backend with CUDA and check VRAM",
      "source": "synthetic",
      "voice": "en_US-amy-medium",
      "expect": { "grammar": null, "critical": ["restart", "backend", "CUDA", "VRAM"] }
    },
    {
      "id": "el-cmd-approve",
      "language": "el",
      "text": "εντάξει",
